node_modules/
# `.env` alone left every sibling copy committable, and this repo is PUBLIC.
# Found 2026-08-02: an untracked `.env.pre-cleanup` (9 lines of tokens/keys,
# left over from the G11 migration) was sitting in the kiosk's checkout, one
# `git add -A` away from being published. Backups are the normal way to edit a
# live .env, so ignore the whole family rather than trusting nobody typos.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.pm2
logs
dist/
.claude/
# Agent scaffolding, all of it local and regenerable. `.agents/` is a MIRROR of
# `.claude/` (same files, s/CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/) and AGENTS.md is CLAUDE.md
# with a different H1 — so tracking them while `.claude/` above is ignored would
# make the copy canonical and let it drift from the original unwatched. It had
# already drifted two days in: the generator's s/.claude/.Codex/ left
# `.agents/skills/audit/SKILL.md` invoking a path that does not exist.
# .codex/ is Codex's own hooks and .gemini/ is Gemini CLI's config plus its
# last review response. None of it is this project's source, and this
# repo is public.
.agents/
.codex/
AGENTS.md
.gemini/
*.env.local
screenshot*.png
.reference/
static/photos/
CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT.md
server/package.json
server/package-lock.json
server/tts-cache/
data/routines/
# Per-install behaviour, same charter as data/routines/ above: this box's own
# depth tallies, meaningless on another wall and not this project's source.
data/census/
data/memories/
data/immich-cache/
data/delight/
data/recipe-cache/
# The photographs the room has said "not this one" to. Per-install judgement,
# not code — and it must never be committed, or one house's vetoes would arrive
# on another's wall (services/photoVeto.js).
data/photos/
# The house knowledge base is a SEPARATE private git repo cloned in here
# (docs/design/VAULT.md). Ignored so the nested clone never shows up as a
# stray gitlink in this repo's status.
data/vault/
# Raw spoken exchanges awaiting consolidation. Short-lived by design (see
# RAW_RETENTION_DAYS in server/services/conversationLog.js) and never, ever
# committed — this repo is public and these are kitchen transcripts.
data/conversations/
# What the house has seen and cannot account for, and its own weather record.
# Camera ids, times, and a daily reading — the house's observations of itself,
# and this repo is public.
data/unresolved.json
data/weather-history.jsonl
# Who was home, day by day (services/occupancyDays.js). It NAMES RESIDENTS and
# this repo is public — the same reason data/unresolved.json above is ignored,
# one notch stronger.
data/occupancy-days.json

# Playwright MCP tool artifacts
.playwright-mcp/
static/js/

# Playwright test artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
# Raw V8 coverage from `npm run verify:v3-coverage` (~40MB, regenerable).
# The conclusions live in docs/design/V3-COVERAGE.md; this is the working data.
coverage/
flag-reversibility-failure.log

# PC-side voice services (Stage B, project-voice-mic-bridge) — venv/models/caches/logs
tools/voice-pc/.venv/
tools/voice-pc/models/
tools/voice-pc/*.log
tools/voice-agent/*.log
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# graphify knowledge-graph output (regenerable; 5.7MB)
graphify-out/
tools/voice-pc/hotwords.txt

# archify visual-check working files (screenshots + receipts)
docs/architecture/*.visual-check.*
